                                                    	                   <h2>Atlantic Cape Baseball</h2>
                                                <p><strong>Be a part of Atlantic Cape Buccaneers Baseball!</strong></p>
<p><img alt="Buccaneers baseball 2026" class="align-right" height="375" src="../../_images/athletics/Baseball-Photos-4-8-2026-6.jpg" width="250"/>Atlantic Cape Community College Buccaneers baseball is part of the National Junior College Athletic Association (NJCAA) Region 19 Division III. Each season gets underway in mid-February and concludes in early-May. The Buccaneers baseball team practices and plays its home games at the College's, state-of-the-art ballfield on the Mays Landing campus.</p>
<p>Are you Interested in playing America's national past-time, baseball, for Atlantic Cape? Prospective student-athletes must be enrolled full time (12 credits) in the Spring Semester and maintain a 2.0 GPA. Must have an updated physical and complete the soccer interest form to participate.</p>
<p><a class="ctaButton" href="https://docs.google.com/forms/d/13esfo-F3G5zo9TqbINEWd7npQYtiiCMX195eh3uH21o/viewform?edit_requested=true" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Please Complete Our Athletics Interest Form!&#160;</a></p>
<p>For more information, contact Athletic Director Jamal Edwards at&#160;<a href="mailto:jedwards@atlanticcape.edu" rel="noopener" target="_blank">jedwards@atlanticcape.edu</a> <br/><a href="../student-athlete-info/index.php">Visit our student-athletes page</a>&#160;for more information on eligibility.</p>
